WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120
I have something I want to teach you

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:06.240
that I've learned through the privilege

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:08.000
of having access to the 0.1%. And I feel

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.080
like this knowledge has been gatekept.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.759
And there are eight things that I've

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.280
identified from these people that I've

00:00:11.759 --> 00:00:15.280
met, that I have worked with, that I

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:18.759
think you can learn from today to make

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.759
your life better.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.840
The first thing I'm going to teach you

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.160
might sound obvious, but give me a

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:31.039
chance to explain it. Every failure is

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.280
one closer step to success. So Richard

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:35.920
Branson for example tells the story

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:39.120
about how he launched Virgin Cola and he

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:41.040
loves to tell how then Coca-Cola came in

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.960
and squashed him. Took all the retail

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:44.879
space away from him by giving bags of

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.879
money to the retail distribution outlets

00:00:44.879 --> 00:00:49.840
and that's it. Virgin Cola came in and

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:51.520
Virgin Cola failed. A massive public

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:53.680
failure. And I think the thing is

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.760
failure is something at school you get

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.440
taught is bad. If you get a D, you're a

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.320
failure. You get drummed into your head

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.879
in school that failure is a bad thing in

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:04.799
a system where you're not rewarded for

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:07.439
failure. But in the real world, I

00:01:04.799 --> 00:01:09.760
wouldn't be the success I am today if I

00:01:07.439 --> 00:01:11.040
hadn't failed many times. I lost a

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.119
million dollars building a business

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.520
called Devshar, a comic business. I lost

00:01:13.119 --> 00:01:17.439
so much time and so much money. And I'm

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:19.439
a guru in business and I failed and I'm

00:01:17.439 --> 00:01:21.119
proud of it. In fact, that comic book is

00:01:19.439 --> 00:01:22.880
in my office on display. It was one of

00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:24.720
my biggest achievements because I tried

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.119
it and it didn't work. It makes me

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:29.119
interesting and it makes it possible for

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:31.119
me to succeed in the future because the

00:01:29.119 --> 00:01:33.040
mistakes I made in that failure I take

00:01:31.119 --> 00:01:34.720
with me to the next thing. Failure is

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:37.040
good. How many businesses fail in the

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:39.119
first year? If you just said 90% in your

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:41.040
head, it's also not true. Failure has

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:42.400
been framed incorrectly. 90% of

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.479
businesses do not fail in the first

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:47.280
year. That is a lie that you have told

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:49.759
yourself is true to stop you starting

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.920
something. 23% of businesses fail in the

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:53.920
first year. 64% of businesses fail

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.280
within the first 3 years. I am part of

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.960
both of these stats. I had a business

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:58.880
that didn't last more than a year, a

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:00.479
gardening company, but I made loads of

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.759
money before it failed. And I made so

00:02:00.479 --> 00:02:03.920
many learnings from that gardening

00:02:01.759 --> 00:02:05.680
company. I was able to go on next and do

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.439
a hotel booking business, which took 3

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:09.280
years to fail. But in that time, I made

00:02:07.439 --> 00:02:10.959
money and then it failed. Don't let

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:13.360
failure be a bad thing. In fact, lean

00:02:10.959 --> 00:02:15.680
into it. Accept the downside and go for

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.760
it anyway. The second thing I've seen in

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:19.360
super successful people, and it's deeply

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.599
in rooted in me as well, we have

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.840
developed a risk muscle. And it does

00:02:21.599 --> 00:02:26.640
take time to develop it like any muscle,

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.720
but risk is a huge part of how we

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.319
operate. An example, I'm launching a

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.480
drinks brand called Dream Brew. Every

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:34.000
can sold, we use the profit we generate

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:35.519
to fund people's dreams. And if you want

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.200
to buy it, the link's down below. This

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:39.200
business not only has taken me a year

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.879
and a half to launch it, but it might

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.760
not work. I'm still going to do it

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:45.519
because all I think about is you got to

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:47.360
put yourself out there and if you're not

00:02:45.519 --> 00:02:49.760
willing to take a risk to do that, then

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:51.920
you won't succeed. It it's similar to

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:55.040
failing like this might fail but the

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:56.640
risk to become a failure I'm also

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:58.800
willing to do. I'm basically taking

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:00.400
action even though I feel it deep in me

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.920
I don't want to take risk and what I've

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.680
discovered the more risk I take the

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.800
luckier I get. The last thing on the

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:06.720
list today I'm going to go through it in

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:08.239
more depth is about luck because there's

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.000
actually a really interesting psychology

00:03:08.239 --> 00:03:11.040
around luck and hacking luck. I'm going

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.120
to talk about it right at the end of

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.159
this video. But you have to believe that

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.680
risk is the right move not no risk. Most

00:03:16.159 --> 00:03:18.959
people I meet on the street when I ask

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.640
them their dream who are miserable or

00:03:18.959 --> 00:03:22.239
people are taking no risk at all.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.280
They're not willing to take a risk.

00:03:22.239 --> 00:03:25.200
They're not willing to go for their

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:26.879
dreams and they go for their whole life

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.480
ending up with regret at the end of the

00:03:26.879 --> 00:03:30.720
journey which is the worst thing to have

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:32.720
regret. And every successful person I've

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:34.400
ever met that's happy has taken a risk

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:36.000
and has a story to tell. And often

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.159
what's really interesting is the

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.080
psychology in humans is because we can

00:03:38.159 --> 00:03:41.599
project the future unlike any other

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.599
animal. We can see what the future might

00:03:41.599 --> 00:03:45.280
look like. We use it against ourselves.

00:03:43.599 --> 00:03:46.720
We project the worst case scenario

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:49.360
instead of the best case scenario. And

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:50.959
nine times out of 10, ironically, the

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:54.080
best case scenario will actually win

00:03:50.959 --> 00:03:56.159
out. All you need to do is learn to put

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.840
your mind in the framework of what's the

00:03:56.159 --> 00:03:59.120
worst that can happen. I started a comic

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:01.360
book business. I lost money I could

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:02.959
afford to lose and I could get a job if

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:04.640
I wanted, I guess, or I just start

00:04:02.959 --> 00:04:06.000
another business. Worst is people around

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.879
me judge me. And if those people are

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.159
judging me, they're not going to be my

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.120
friends anyway. So, I'm happy to lose

00:04:08.159 --> 00:04:10.560
those people if they're going to judge

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:12.959
me for that. Right. The next thing I've

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:15.040
