00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:16.319
greener on the other side. It's greener

00:08:14.639 --> 00:08:17.840
where you water it. And if you get your

00:08:16.319 --> 00:08:20.160
partnerships right, both business

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:22.479
partnerships and life partnerships, you

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:24.160
can get your whole life on track. And

00:08:22.479 --> 00:08:25.919
it's so underlooked because in school

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:27.520
they'll tell you to sit and do an exam

00:08:25.919 --> 00:08:29.120
on your own. That getting an A on your

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:31.520
own is success and getting a D is

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:33.360
failure. In the real world, everybody's

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:35.039
successful. It's doing it in armies.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:36.640
They're doing it in tribes. They're

00:08:35.039 --> 00:08:38.240
doing it in communities. And you need to

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:40.000
learn to do the same. The next trait

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:42.719
I've seen from successful people is

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:44.240
follow through. You've got to have grit.

00:08:42.719 --> 00:08:46.080
I always tell people who want to be

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:48.000
successful, wanting it not enough.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:49.760
You've got to need it. And successful

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:51.279
people, they don't just want it, they

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:53.200
need it. Now sometimes they use their

00:08:51.279 --> 00:08:54.640
ego to fuel that need and other times

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:56.720
they're solving a problem in the world.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:58.959
That means I have to follow through. Now

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:00.720
